critic.task_types:
Our 30 exam tasks (I read all ten topics' K-sections): K1 = error-spotting x4, true/false with justification x4, table completion x2. K2 = comparison by perspectives x5, table completion x3, material analysis x1, theory application x1. K3 = material analysis x6, ethical analysis x3, theory application x1. All 30 use fictional text material without numbers, so the material share is about 90%. That is higher than the real exam's 64%, but the material type differs: real exams use charts, maps, statistics tables, a hypnogram, product labels, images and video (about 18 of 72 tasks), and we have none of these. Six of our ten K3 tasks share one template (analyse levels 10 p, mechanism 8 p, evaluate plus two proposals 12 p), which is monotone. The real exam scores 20 p and 30 p tasks as half content and half tiedonkäsittely (information processing: concept use, analysis, evaluation, argumentation). Material tasks lose 5 p if the answer does not refer to the material.

Real types missing from our tasks:
- list-and-classify with a count rubric (S23-2, S23-3, S25-2);
- name the concept for 20 definitions (S25-1);
- multiple choice with penalty marking (A25-1, A26-1) and drop-down cloze (A26-2);
- define-and-exemplify (A23-2, A25-2, A25-3);
- draw a model (A23-3.1) or a chart from a table (S24-9.1, S25-7.1);
- read a hypnogram, map, chart or labels;
- apply a supplied framework table (the WHO action areas);
- critique a concept (S26-3.2);
- a justify-why essay without material (S25-5, S26-6);
- video material;
- a research plan (S26-9, TE2).

The 'recall' formats (true/false on nutrients, concept naming, multiple choice) demand specific facts our pages avoid.

What to change:
(1) Vary the K3 template and add a separate content and tiedonkäsittely scoring line, plus the material-use deduction, to model answers. Add one shared rubric page.
(2) Give at least three topics a data K-task: te1-01 a population table or chart by group, te1-05 a hypnogram, te1-04 product labels. Numbers in data are compatible with the safe-messaging rule if they are population statistics, not personal targets.
(3) Add a draw-and-explain task in te1-02 and a chart-drawing task in te1-01.
(4) Add a WHO action-area application task in te1-01 (or te1-04 or te1-10).
(5) Add at least one list-and-classify, one define-and-exemplify and one multiple-choice-with-penalty task across the set.
(6) Keep error-spotting and theory application: both match real tasks (S26-1, A26-4, S26-4, A26-5).
